# Every scratch build a shot script makes. It was two names, and the third
# script to need one (scripts/shot-idle-page.mjs, w-73c319c398) would have
# committed four directories of built renderer.

renderer/dist-*/
shots/ck/*.png
# The before/after run of scripts/prove-z-takes-the-task-back.mjs (w-d853a1a136).
# Regenerated by the script; the pair she was shown is in the product's docs.
renderer/shots-z/
# The timings scripts/measure-the-code-pane-lag.mjs writes (w-c1d09f0638). One
# json per commit per throttle rate, regenerated by re-running it; the numbers
# she was shown are in the product's docs.
shots-lag/
shots-before/
shots-after/

# The packaged app. Hundreds of megabytes, rebuilt by `npm run release`.
release/
# The 2048px drawings behind the icon, redrawn by `npm run icon`. The .icns they
# produce IS committed: without it there is no build, and rebuilding it needs a
# Mac with a screen.
build/icons/
renderer/shots-tab/
# Where the shot scripts drop frames when nobody names an out directory. Fifty
# seven of these went into a commit by accident on w-cf0e8821b3: they are the
# app photographed, so they belong in the product's docs where she reads them,
# never in the source tree.
designs-out/

# THE 3456x2304 THEME SOURCES ARE NOT IN GIT, and that is a decision rather
# than an oversight (w-a863b48784, 2026-08-21). Fifteen PNGs at that size are
# 177 MB, against about 2 MB for each earlier round, and git keeps them
# forever. What is tracked instead: the shipped .webp files themselves
# (renderer/src/assets), every prompt and usage record beside the PNGs, and
# scripts/theme-images-hi.mjs, which redraws them from the round-four and
# round-five PNGs that ARE tracked. The PNGs stay on this machine.
designs/w-a863b48784/raw-hi/*.png

# A GIT WORKTREE MADE INSIDE THE CHECKOUT INSTEAD OF IN /tmp (w-1aa8351b19,
# 2026-08-24). Two were sitting in wt/, carrying 376 test files of somebody's
# half-finished branch. vitest.config.mjs is what stops the suite running them.
# This is what stops `git add -A` committing them.
wt/

# The window helper is compiled from main/window-helper.swift by
# scripts/build-window-helper.mjs on every build. A checked-in binary is a thing
# nobody can review and everybody has to trust.
main/window-helper
shots-w/

# The before/after shots and frame timings from w-481e93b9eb, 2026-09-18.
shots-glass/
renderer/dist-glass/

# The before/after shots of the open pane from w-0c451019f1, 2026-09-20.
shots-live-pane/
renderer/dist-live/

# ONE-OFF HARNESSES GO HERE AND STAY OUT OF GIT.
#
# Proving a change in this app means booting it against a throwaway store,
# driving it and photographing the window, so a session writes a little script
# to do that. The picture is the deliverable and it goes to the product's
# documents. The script is scaffolding: it runs once and never again.
#
# 226 of them had been committed by 2026-09-23, none referenced by anything,
# and one of them was where a real account id came back into the tree a day
# after it had been cleaned out. Write them here instead. A harness that turns
# out to be worth keeping can be moved up into scripts/ deliberately, which is
# the only way one should ever get there.
scripts/scratch/

# THE OPERATOR'S OWN STANDING INSTRUCTIONS ARE NOT SOURCE.
#
# `briefs/founder.md` is whatever the person running this app types into the
# Standing instructions box. It is theirs, it is about their work, and it has
# no business in a public repository. It was tracked because a worker can write
# files in this checkout and git made a quiet rewrite visible; that reason is
# real but it is not worth publishing somebody's notes to keep.
#
# Nothing breaks without it. The app reads the copy in its own data folder
# (`app.getPath('userData')/briefs/founder.md`), `carryHerBriefsAcross` only
# seeds that from here when the data folder has none, and `standingInstructions`
# treats a missing file as no instructions at all.
briefs/founder.md

# THE TEAM CLOUD'S ADDRESS AND KEY ARE NOT SOURCE EITHER.
#
# `cloud/team.config.json` points the team version at one hosted project. It
# lives only on the machines that run that version; a checkout without it is
# the single-person app. `cloud/team.config.example.json` shows the shape.
cloud/team.config.json
